<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nationalist faction (Spanish Civil War)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1936–1939</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nationalists were the side in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-civil-war">Spanish Civil War</a> that rose against the Second Spanish Republic in July 1936, uniting army officers, the Falange, monarchists, Carlists and conservative Catholics. Led from October 1936 by General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-franco">Francisco Franco</a> and aided by Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascist-italy">Fascist Italy</a>, they won the war in April 1939. Their victory established Franco's dictatorship, which lasted until his death in 1975.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nationalist-faction-spanish-civil-war.jpg" alt="Nationalist faction (Spanish Civil War)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Durero · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Bando_Nacional_(1936%E2%80%931938).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
